WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.375
Why does this need care?

2
00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:06.187
Microsoft Learn's workload identity
federation documentation explains it.

3
00:00:06.187 --> 00:00:10.732
A federated credential tells Microsoft
Entra I D to trust tokens from

4
00:00:10.732 --> 00:00:14.963
an outside issuer, such as GitHub
Actions or a Kubernetes cluster.

5
00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:20.897
Three values must match the workload's
token exactly, case for case: the issuer,

6
00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:26.090
the subject, and the audience, which
for Entra I D is exactly one value,

7
00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.613
A P I colon slash slash
Azure A D Token Exchange.

8
00:00:29.613 --> 00:00:31.351
And here's the quiet failure.

9
00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:35.738
Learn says a credential with the wrong
subject is created without any error.

10
00:00:35.738 --> 00:00:39.379
It fails only when the workload
tries to exchange its token,

11
00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:41.312
which may be the day you cut over.

12
00:00:41.312 --> 00:00:45.993
So in this module, each federated credential
is checked against the claims the

13
00:00:45.993 --> 00:00:49.810
workload will present, and tested
against a fake token endpoint,

14
00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.310
before it's ever created.
